"SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0" and a header describing the changes.

  separate.py  vocal separation with Demucs (htdemucs). Ported from
               app/services/audio.py (_DEMUCS_SCRIPT, separate_vocals).
               Modified: standalone script; also writes the accompaniment;
               progress lines on stderr; one JSON line as the result;
               exit code 1 on failure.
  analyze.py   vocal-based scene segmentation (5-10 s scenes from silence,
               vocal valleys, breaths, bars and section changes, joined by
               dynamic programming). Ported from app/services/audio.py
               (analyze_boundaries, plan_scenes) and
               docs/vocal-scene-segmentation.md. Modified: standalone script
               with JSON output; the first and last boundaries are never moved
               by candidate merging; fallback to an even split when no path
               exists; instrumental detection (has_vocals).

Demucs, PyTorch, librosa and the other packages these scripts use are not
included in this repository. `setup --mv` installs them into
components/mvtools/.venv from PyPI and download.pytorch.org under their own
licenses.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
studio/mvscript.py, studio/mvclip.py
----------------------------------------------------------------------
These files are also ported from Minimax-H3-lipsync-mv, Copyright 2026 YUZUKI,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and have been modified. They
remain under the Apache License, Version 2.0; each file carries
"SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0" and a header describing the changes.

  mvscript.py  scene-by-scene direction for the MV: the scenario request with
               one JSON-repair turn, the identity / subject text, frame-kind
               guidance, the six-section MiniMax-H3 Ref2VA prompt formatter and
               the lip-sync enforcement. Ported from app/services/llm.py
               (_extract_json, _scenario_request, _identity_instruction,
               _subject_definition, frame_kind, _FRAME_LLM_GUIDANCE,
               _BACKGROUND_TEXT_GUIDANCE, _FRAME_SHOT_PREFIX,
               format_h3_official_ref2va_prompt,
               enforce_reference_and_lipsync, generate_scenario).
               Modified: async calls to this studio's single-turn LLM client;
               JSON extraction prefers objects; narration branches and
               analyze_character are not ported here (analyze_character is
               in mvdescribe.py below); an unreadable overview does not
               stop the run.
  mvclip.py    frame-grid quantization of the scene plan, per-scene seeds and
               the ffmpeg command lines that fit a clip to its exact length
               and join the clips under the original song. Ported from
               app/services/audio.py (quantize_scene_plan), app/pipeline.py
               (per-scene seed) and app/services/h3.py (finish_scene,
               concatenate_and_mux). Modified: the commands are only built here
               (run by studio/handlers/mv.py); a clip that H3 returns short is
               padded by cloning its last frame.

